// niri's config: yours. nemo adds itself with the one include line below: its niri look, keys,
// window rules, colours and screens, written by the shell into ~/.config/nemo/niri (each part can be
// switched off in nemo's settings → system → niri). What you write after that line wins.
// The niri wiki: https://yalter.github.io/niri/Configuration:-Introduction

// nemo: its niri look, keys, window rules, colours and screens (~/.config/nemo/niri).
// What you write below wins. `nemo niri disconnect` takes these lines out.
include optional=true "~/.config/nemo/niri/nemo.kdl"

// ─── your settings ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// for example:
//   input { keyboard { repeat-rate 30; } }
//   binds { Mod+Return { spawn "foot"; } }
